; 07-instantiate-a-universal-fact.kurt
;
; Instantiate a universal fact
;
; Load `logic` for quantifier inference rules. A universally quantified fact can be instantiated
; at a particular value:

load logic
prop P
const P, c

use forall $x P($x)
P(c)

; `$x` is the bound variable. A symbol starting with `$` (or `%` for a formula) is always a
; variable, no matter what (see keywords/06-var.kurt). Instantiating it is built into Kurt, so
; `P(c)` follows directly from the fact and the output shows just `by 12`.
